254: ## Secrets and history rewrites
255: 
256: | Date | What leaked into a run log | Fix |
257: |---|---|---|
258: | 2026-11-19 | Environment variables printed by AndroidWorld's setup (an API key, a session token) | Redacted in every commit (`git filter-branch`) |
259: | 2026-11-20 | An expired Colab file-proxy token inside a download URL | Redacted in every commit (`git filter-branch`) |
260: 
261: - **Hash maps:** old → new commit hashes are in [history-rewrites.md](history-rewrites.md).
262: - **Scan:** two independent scans (ours and Codex's) found no credentials. They covered every file in every commit
263:   reachable from `main` and the archive tag, including compressed episode files.
264:   - Checked: cloud keys, Hugging Face / OpenAI / Anthropic / GitHub / Google / Modal tokens, private keys, JWTs and
265:     key/token/secret/password assignments.
266:   - Not checked: images (no OCR).
267: - **Owner identity:** the owner's git e-mail appears in commit author fields and in Codex logs that captured `git log`.
268: - **Automatic redaction on commit (limited).** `.gitattributes` runs the `redact-env` clean filter on `*.log` files
269:   only, and only where it is configured locally:
270:   - It redacts `'NAME_WITH_KEY|TOKEN|SECRET|PASSWORD': '…'` pairs (the format AndroidWorld prints) and JWT-shaped
271:     tokens.
272:   - It does **not** catch other formats (e.g. `HF_TOKEN=…`, lowercase JSON keys).
273:   - Run a scan before publishing. One-time setup:
274: 
275: ```bash
276: git config filter.redact-env.clean "LC_ALL=C sed -E -e \"s/'([A-Z0-9_]*(KEY|TOKEN|SECRET|PASSWORD)[A-Z0-9_]*)': '[^']*'/'\\\\1': '<redacted>'/g\" -e 's/eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{15,}[.]eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{15,}[.][A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}/<redacted-token>/g'"
277: git config filter.redact-env.smudge cat
278: ```
