1: # History rewrites
2: 
3: Two rewrites removed credentials from committed run logs. Nothing else changed: each final tree is identical apart
4: from the redacted text. Commit hashes cited in older files (Codex prompts and reports, PREREG) map as below; commit
5: subjects are shortened.
6: 
7: ## 2026-11-20 (~12:30 Asia/Manila): expired Colab proxy token
8: 
9: A Codex audit log (`logs/codex_mw_r2_audit.log`) and an upload log (`logs/colab_upload_maiui_q8.log`) contained a
10: download URL with a Colab file-proxy token (a JWT scoped to the Colab T4 VM that served the MobileWorld models; it
11: had expired on 2026-11-18 21:54 UTC and the VM no longer exists). Every commit from old `f76ba4d` on was rewritten with
12: `git filter-branch` to replace it with `<redacted-token>`. The local `redact-env` clean filter (`*.log` only) now also
13: redacts JWT-shaped tokens; see [repository.md](repository.md#secrets-and-history-rewrites) for what it does not catch.
