FILE README.md (107 lines)
1: # LFM3-VL-2B Android agent
2: 
3: Post-training LiquidAI **LFM3-VL-2B** into a small, screenshot-only Android agent that runs on the phone, then
4: comparing it fairly with **GUI-Owl-1.5-2B** and **MAI-UI-2B**.
5: 
6: | | |
7: |---|---|
8: | Final model | **LFM3-VL-2B v4**: LoRA fine-tune, shipped as a 4-bit GGUF (1.30 GB with its image projector) |
9: | Main benchmark | AndroidWorld, 3 held-out seeds × 116 tasks, **preregistered** ([docs/PREREG_v4.md](docs/PREREG_v4.md)) |
10: | Other benchmarks | MobileWorld (105 tasks), AndroidControl (offline), speed on CPU, Apple M5 and a phone |
11: | Status | Complete (2026-11-19). Every result was independently re-checked by Codex ([docs/audits.md](docs/audits.md)) |
12: 
13: ## Results at a glance
14: 
15: ### AndroidWorld, held-out seeds (primary, preregistered)
16: 
17: Same harness for every model: 1 screenshot per step, 4-bit model via llama.cpp, same step budget, temperature 0.
18: 
19: | Model | Seed 7 | Seed 1234 | Seed 2026 | **Total / 348** |
20: |---|---|---|---|---|
21: | **LFM3-VL-2B v4 (ours)** | 18 | 17 | 19 | **54 (15.5%)** |
22: | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | 16 | 13 | 18 | 47 (13.5%) |
23: | LFM3-VL-2B v1 (our first model) | 11 | 10 | 11 | 32 (9.2%) |
24: 
25: - **v4 vs GUI-Owl: +2.0 points, 95% CI [−4.5, +8.6], p = 0.60.** Non-inferior at the preregistered −6.9-point
26:   margin. Superiority is **not** shown.
27: - **v4 vs v1: +6.3 points, 95% CI [+1.1, +11.5], p = 0.02.**
28: - The non-inferiority result depends on the preregistered rule that re-runs an episode once if the emulator crashed
29:   before step 1. 113 of v4's seed-1234 episodes needed it after one emulator hung overnight. Counting them as
30:   failures instead gives −2.9 points (not non-inferior).
31: - **v4's lead comes from templates whose goal text cannot change with the seed.** Seed 30 was used to pick v4. On
32:   the 78 templates whose goal text does change, v4 and GUI-Owl are level: 32 vs 33, CI [−8.2, +7.3], so
33:   non-inferiority is not shown on that subset.
34: - Codex audit: **valid with caveats**. The caveats:
35:   - device state carries over between episodes (all models);
36:   - two disputed checker successes, one v4 and one v1 (counting both as failures leaves the conclusion unchanged);
37:   - limited power: about 57% to show non-inferiority if the models are truly equal.
38: 
39: ### MobileWorld (secondary, descriptive; one run per model)
40: 
41: | Model | Successes / 105 |
42: |---|---|
43: | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | **22 (21.0%)** |
44: | MAI-UI-2B | 11 (10.5%) |
45: | LFM3-VL-2B v4 | 6 (5.7%) |
46: 
47: - GUI-Owl is clearly better here: v4 − GUI-Owl = −15.2 points, exact McNemar p = 3.05 × 10⁻⁵.
48: - MAI-UI − v4 = +4.8 points (p = 0.18). MAI-UI's run had more environment failures; see [docs/results.md](docs/results.md#mobileworld).
49: 
50: ### Speed (median seconds per step; small pilot measurements)
51: 
52: | Hardware | **v4** | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | MAI-UI-2B |
53: |---|---|---|---|
54: | CPU, 8 threads (Intel Xeon, idle VM); 4-bit; calls kept 14 / 4 / 4 | **6.4** | 58.0 | 58.2 |
55: | Apple M5 GPU, every step of the seed-30 runs (1,706–2,228 steps each) | **2.96** | 7.00 | 9.35 (8-bit) |
56: | Phone CPU (Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6), as evaluated; calls 10 / 2 / 2 | **~39** | ~1,100 | ~1,063 (8-bit) |
57: 
58: - In the CPU test v4 used about a third as many prompt tokens per step (a smaller image) and showed about 3× the
59:   prompt throughput. The tests compare whole pipelines and do not isolate the cause.
60: - At an equal 1,024-token image ceiling on the phone, GUI-Owl and MAI-UI take ~198 s and ~183 s; their accuracy
61:   at that ceiling was not measured.
62: 
63: ### Development seed 30 (used to pick versions, so not evidence)
64: 
65: | v4 | MAI-UI-2B | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | Qwen3.5-2B v1 | LFM3 v1 | LFM3 v3 | LFM3 v2 |
66: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
67: | 18 | **32** | 23 | 16 | 15 | 13 | 3 |
68: 
69: MAI-UI-2B (8-bit, 1 screenshot) scored highest on the development seed but was **not** run on the held-out seeds.
70: 
