8: ## Versions at a glance
9: 
10: AndroidWorld = development seed 30, successes out of 116 ([results.md](results.md#androidworld-development-seed-30)).
11: 
12: | Version | What changed | AndroidWorld | Lesson |
13: |---|---|---|---|
14: | **v1** | AndroidControl only (official train episodes) | 15 | Strong at acting; never uses `answer` |
15: | **v2** | + GUI-Odyssey, AMEX, ScreenQA | 3 | 8,739 rows had a **blank intent**: a suspected cause (the data mix also changed) |
16: | v2 + forced intent | Inference-only test: force a one-line intent | 6 | Supports the blank-intent suspicion, but small: 3 wins, 0 losses, paired p = 0.25 |
17: | v1 + runtime feedback | Inference-only test: app-name resolution + failure notes | 10 | Worse; dropped |
18: | **v3** | v2 mix with blank intents filled (2,603 by action templates, 6,106 by a teacher model; 30 rows dropped) | 13 | Offline gains on the new datasets did not transfer to AndroidWorld |
19: | v4 (first build) | First v4 dataset | — | Codex data audit said STOP (answer leaks, guard gaps); run abandoned, retrained on rebuilt data |
20: | **v4 (final)** | v3 data in the v4 prompt + navigate-then-answer episodes + installed-app list + shorter ScreenQA answers | **18** | Fixed "never answers" (0 → 6 answer tasks); passed the gate; frozen |
21: | v4-RL | 200 steps of GRPO on static screenshots, from v4 | not run | Failed its offline promotion rule |
22: 
23: Other base models on v1's data: Qwen3.5-2B with the same recipe (16); Qwen3.5-0.8B and LFM2.5-VL-450M with a
24: smaller one (LoRA r16, 1 epoch): 12 and 2.
25: 
26: ---
27: 
28: ## Training recipe
29: 
30: The LFM3-VL-2B SFT runs v1–v4 share this recipe and target budget, so data and prompt are the intended variables.
31: Per-run deviations (resumes, checkpoint cadence) are listed under [Training runs](#training-runs).
32: 
33: | Setting | Value |
34: |---|---|
35: | Method | LoRA SFT on the language model only; vision tower frozen |
36: | LoRA | rank 64, alpha 128; attention, MLP and convolution projections |
37: | Optimiser | lr 2e-4, 1,250 steps × 32 rows (batch 8 × gradient accumulation 4) |
38: | Image | One screenshot per step, area budget 880 × 880 px (≈ 720 image tokens for a phone screen) |
39: | Input | Goal + text history of earlier steps + current screenshot (v4: + installed-app list) |
40: | Output | `<think>short intent</think>` + one JSON action, coordinates on a 0–1000 grid |
41: | Checkpoints | Pushed to the Hub so a lost VM can resume: every 100 steps (v1, LFM2.5-VL-450M), 50 steps (all later runs) |
42: 
43: Code: [`train/sft_vlm.py`](../train/sft_vlm.py), prompt and action format in
44: [`train/agent_format.py`](../train/agent_format.py), job configs in
45: [`scripts/training/jobs/`](../scripts/training/jobs/).
46: 
47: ### Action space
48: 
49: `click`, `long_press`, `input_text` (types, then presses Enter), `scroll` (up/down/left/right), `open_app`,
50: `navigate_back`, `navigate_home`, `keyboard_enter`, `wait`, `answer` (v4), `status` (`complete` / `infeasible`).
51: 
