FILE docs/evaluation.md (172 lines)
1: # How the benchmarks were run
2: 
3: **Contents:** [Fairness at a glance](#fairness-at-a-glance) · [AndroidWorld](#androidworld) ·
4: [MobileWorld](#mobileworld) · [AndroidControl](#androidcontrol-offline) ·
5: [General knowledge](#general-knowledge-retention) · [Speed](#speed)
6: 
7: ---
8: 
9: ## Fairness at a glance
10: 
11: ### AndroidWorld (primary comparison: v4 vs GUI-Owl)
12: 
13: | Setting | v4 | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | Same? |
14: |---|---|---|---|
15: | Tasks, seeds, emulator image, harness | AndroidWorld, 116 tasks × seeds 7/1234/2026 | same | yes |
16: | Screenshots per step | 1 | 1 | yes |
17: | Step budget, temperature | 10 × task complexity, 0 | same | yes |
18: | Weights | 4-bit (Q4_K_M) | 4-bit (Q4_K_M) | yes |
19: | Installed-app list in the prompt | yes | yes | yes |
20: | Image size | ≤ 880×880 px area (≈ 720 tokens) | ≤ 1,048,576 px (≈ 1,024 tokens) | no: GUI-Owl gets a larger image |
21: | Prompt and output format | its own (trained) | its official one, ported | no |
22: | Parse retries | 1 | 0 (an unparseable reply wastes the step) | no |
23: | AndroidWorld in training data | none (contamination rule) | undisclosed by its authors | unknown |
24: 
25: GUI-Owl is not run in its published setup (5 screenshots at full resolution). That setup took 61 s per step on the
26: M5 (~10,700 prompt tokens), so a full 116-task run would take about two days per seed. The project targets an
27: on-device budget of one screenshot.
28: 
29: ### MobileWorld (secondary)
30: 
31: | Setting | v4 | GUI-Owl / MAI-UI |
32: |---|---|---|
33: | Agent | our adapter | MobileWorld's official agents |
34: | Screenshots per step | 1 | 1 |
35: | Image | ≤ 880×880 px area, ≤ 1,024 tokens | full screenshot, ≤ 2,600 tokens |
36: | Weights | 4-bit | GUI-Owl 4-bit; MAI-UI 8-bit (its 4-bit output degenerates) |
37: 
38: The larger image budgets give GUI-Owl and MAI-UI more visual detail; their effect on accuracy was not isolated.
39: 
40: ---
41: 
42: ## AndroidWorld
43: 
44: ### Setup (all models)
45: 
46: | Item | Setting |
47: |---|---|
48: | Benchmark | AndroidWorld @ `55ddaf5` + local patches (below); 116 task templates, 1 instance each |
49: | Device | Pixel 6 AVD, Android 13 (API 33, arm64); two emulators (ports 5556, 5558) on an Apple M5 Mac |
50: | Model server | llama.cpp `llama-server` on Metal, one request at a time |
51: | Weights | 4-bit (Q4_K_M) + 8-bit image projector; MAI-UI 8-bit (Q8_0) |
52: | Step budget | AndroidWorld default: 10 × task complexity |
53: | Decoding | Temperature 0 |
54: | Seeds | Development: 30. Held-out: 7, 1234, 2026 |
55: | Success | Checker score ≥ 1 **and** the agent ended the episode. Exceptions are failures |
56: 
57: ### Per-model settings (held-out runs)
58: 
59: | | v4 | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (matched) | v1 |
60: |---|---|---|---|
61: | Agent code | `eval/androidworld/lfm_agent.py`, prompt v4 | `eval/androidworld/guiowl_agent.py` (official prompt, ported) | `lfm_agent.py`, original prompt |
62: | Screenshots per step | 1 | 1 | 1 |
63: | Image | ≤ 880×880 px area (≈ 720 tokens; server cap 1,024) | ≤ 1,048,576 px (≈ 1,024 tokens; server cap 2,600 not reached) | as v4 |
64: | Context window | 8,192 | 20,480 | 8,192 |
65: | Installed-app list | yes | yes | no |
66: | Output | `<think>intent</think>` + one JSON action | `Action:` + `<tool_call>` | as v4 |
67: 
68: Launcher with the exact flags: [`scripts/androidworld/local_sealed_aw_v3.sh`](../scripts/androidworld/local_sealed_aw_v3.sh).
69: 
70: ### Local patches to AndroidWorld
71: 
72: Files: `eval/androidworld/android_world_local_fixes.patch`, `eval/androidworld/android_env_no_adb_kill.patch`.
73: None touches model input/output or scoring.
74: 
75: - App launch works on software-key emulators (`monkey --pct-syskeys 0`).
76: - The shared adb server is never killed; optional adb server port.
77: - Directory cleanup is verified; a failed cleanup fails the attempt.
78: - A crash in `tear_down` is recorded on the episode instead of stopping the suite.
79: - Resume keeps saved exception episodes as failures; checkpoints are written atomically.
80: 
81: ### Held-out protocol (preregistered)
82: 
83: - **Sealed:** results went to `results/androidworld_sealed/`; only episode counts were checked until every model
84:   had finished that seed.
85: - **Re-run rule:** an infrastructure crash before step 1 (emulator/adb, not model output) is re-run once.
86:   Everything else counts as it is.
87: - **Trajectory review:** checker successes are compared with their saved screenshots (done for all v4 and GUI-Owl
88:   successes and v1's on seeds 1234/2026). Contradicted successes are listed in `results/aw_checker_disputes.json`
89:   and enter only a sensitivity analysis.
90: - **Primary analysis:** paired difference v4 − GUI-Owl over 348 instances; template-clustered sign-flip test
91:   (10,000 draws, seed 0); 95% CI by test inversion.
92: - **Decision rule:** non-inferior if the CI's lower bound is above −6.9 points (8 tasks of 116).
93: - **Development gate:** v4 had to pass a gate on seed 30 and offline checks before it could run held-out. It passed.
94: 
95: Full text and every dated change: [PREREG_v4.md](PREREG_v4.md).
96: 
97: ---
98: 
99: ## MobileWorld
100: 
101: | Item | Setting |
102: |---|---|
103: | Benchmark | MobileWorld @ `a026188`, 105 English GUI-only tasks |
104: | Environment | Official Docker image (`ghcr.io/tongyi-mai/mobile_world`), on a GCP n2-standard-16 spot VM with nested virtualisation |
105: | Model servers | llama.cpp `cd959bae9` on a Colab T4 GPU, reached through a restricted reverse SSH tunnel |
106: | Task settings | 50 rounds, 3 s step wait, `--auto_retry 3`, temperature 0 |
107: | v4 agent | Our adapter: `eval/mobileworld/lfm3_mw_agent.py` |
108: | GUI-Owl agent | MobileWorld's official `gui_owl_1_5` agent |
109: | MAI-UI agent | MobileWorld's official agent, 1 screenshot (`eval/mobileworld/maiui_mw_agent.py`) |
110: 
111: **Completion rule** (fixed 2026-11-19 01:55, before any re-run outcome; in
112: [`scripts/mobileworld/gcp_mw_resume_vm.sh`](../scripts/mobileworld/gcp_mw_resume_vm.sh)):
113: 
114: | Task ended because… | Handling |
115: |---|---|
116: | Setup or scoring failed (HTTP 500 from the environment) | One more invocation in a freshly restarted container (up to 4 executions inside it) |
117: | VM stop or preemption cut it off, or never reached | Run it |
118: | Model server unreachable (added before MAI-UI started) | Run it |
119: | Unsupported action, unparseable output, `ask_user` without a simulator | Failure |
120: 
121: MAI-UI ran in two halves (53/52 tasks, alternating) in parallel containers, after GUI-Owl and v4 had finished.
122: 
123: ---
124: 
125: ## AndroidControl (offline)
126: 
127: | Item | Setting |
128: |---|---|
129: | Data | Official **test** episodes: 1,543 episodes, 8,444 steps |
130: | Modes | High-level (goal + history → action; headline), low-level (+ step instruction), terminal rows (→ `complete`) |
131: | History | Teacher-forced (human step instructions + ground-truth actions); an upper bound on closed-loop behaviour |
132: | Generation | Greedy, ≤ 256 new tokens, bf16 on GPU (`eval/androidcontrol/generate.py`) |
133: | Scoring | `eval/androidcontrol/score.py`; unparseable output = wrong |
134: 
135: Step success rate counts a step correct if the action type matches and:
136: 
137: | Action | Correct if |
138: |---|---|
139: | click, long_press | Point inside the target element's box, or within 14% of the screen of the true point |
140: | input_text | Normalised exact match or token F1 ≥ 0.5 |
141: | scroll | Same direction |
142: | open_app | Case-insensitive match or containment |
143: | back, home, wait | Type match is enough |
144: 
145: Development splits (GUI-Odyssey, AMEX, ScreenQA, v4 questions) use the same scorer; see [datasets.md](datasets.md).
146: 
147: ---
148: 
149: ## General knowledge (retention)
150: 
151: - MMStar (1,500 questions) and MMLU (1,000), forced-choice next-token scoring (independent of output format).
152: - Each fine-tune is compared with its base model on the same questions (paired, exact McNemar).
153: - Code: `eval/general/eval_general.py`, `eval/general/paired_retention.py`.
154: 
155: ---
156: 
157: ## Speed
158: 
159: | Measurement | How |
160: |---|---|
161: | CPU | 5 screenshots, 1 warm-up + 3 passes, 8 threads; cached calls excluded (14 / 4 / 4 kept) |
162: | Apple M5 | Model time per step recorded inside the AndroidWorld seed-30 runs, while emulators and other servers were running |
163: | Phone | Model runs on the phone's CPU (4 threads); 2 calls per model at the evaluation ceiling, 2 × 5 calls at the equal ceiling |
164: 
165: - **CPU host:** idle GCP n2-standard-16; each model's own evaluation agent; [`scripts/speed/bench_speed.sh`](../scripts/speed/bench_speed.sh).
166: - **Phone:** Qualcomm reference phone via Qualcomm Device Cloud; llama.cpp b12110, RAM prompt cache off; model files
167:   checked by SHA-256; [`scripts/speed/qdc_chain2.sh`](../scripts/speed/qdc_chain2.sh).
168: 
169: Phone caveats:
170: - Frequencies are sampled, not controlled.
171: - GUI-Owl and MAI-UI reused cached system-prompt tokens, which favours them.
172: - v4's agent sends a 576×1280 screenshot; the others send 1080×2400.
FILE docs/infrastructure.md (66 lines)
1: # Infrastructure and incidents
2: 
3: **Contents:** [Where things ran](#where-things-ran) · [Cost controls](#cost-controls) · [Incidents](#incidents-and-fixes) ·
4: [Lessons](#lessons)
5: 
6: ---
7: 
8: ## Where things ran
9: 
10: | Work | Hardware |
11: |---|---|
12: | SFT v1, v3, LFM2.5-VL-450M | Modal GPU containers (A100 / H100) |
13: | SFT Qwen3.5-2B / 0.8B, v2 mixes | Google Colab GPUs |
14: | SFT v4, offline evals, v4-RL (GRPO) | Colab A100-40GB |
15: | AndroidWorld: every seed-30 and held-out run | Apple M5 Mac, 2 Android emulators (Pixel 6, API 33, arm64), llama.cpp on Metal |
16: | MobileWorld v4 run 1 (discarded) | AWS EC2 `c8i.4xlarge` (nested virtualisation), model on CPU |
17: | MobileWorld run 2: GUI-Owl, v4, MAI-UI | GCP `n2-standard-16` spot VM (nested virtualisation); models on a Colab T4 through a reverse SSH tunnel restricted to the model ports |
18: | CPU speed benchmark | The same GCP VM, idle, before its MobileWorld run |
19: | Phone speed benchmark | Qualcomm Device Cloud (Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6 reference phone); earlier attempt on a Pixel 9 via Firebase device streaming |
20: | Audits and research | Codex CLI on the Mac |
21: 
22: Colab VMs have no KVM, so Android emulators could not run there. That is why MobileWorld moved to AWS and GCP.
23: 
24: ---
25: 
26: ## Cost controls
27: 
28: - Every cloud VM powers itself off after 12 h (AWS `shutdown -h`, GCP `--max-run-duration`).
29: - Colab sessions were stopped by a watchdog once their jobs finished.
30: - The whole pipeline was smoke-tested before any paid run (rule adopted after an early v3 attempt failed inside a
31:   paid pipeline).
32: 
33: ---
34: 
35: ## Incidents and fixes
36: 
37: | When (Manila) | Incident | Handling |
38: |---|---|---|
39: | 11-16/17 | Early v3 attempt failed inside its paid pipeline | Rule: smoke-test the whole pipeline before paid compute |
40: | 11-17 | v2 scored 3/116 | Blank intents suspected (forcing an intent: 3 → 6, p = 0.25); v3 filled them |
41: | 11-18 04:51 | Colab A100 VM lost during v4 SFT (step 353) | Resumed from the step-350 Hub checkpoint on a new A100; training refuses to restart from scratch if a checkpoint exists |
42: | 11-18 06:25 | Answer check accepted padded answers ("12M is incorrect") | Stricter gate criterion, fixed before any v4 result |
43: | 11-18 08:10 | Hugging Face private storage full; merged v4 upload failed | Weights copied off the VM and verified tensor by tensor; the v2 dataset was made public to free space |
44: | 11-18 09:30 | Resuming an AndroidWorld run would retry saved exceptions | Patched: saved failures stay failures; checkpoints written atomically |
45: | 11-18 11:20 | GUI-Owl on CPU ≈ 45–58 s per step | Served from a Colab GPU through a tunnel |
46: | 11-18 13:50 | llama.cpp's RAM prompt cache served repeated screenshots in the speed test | Cached calls excluded from the statistics |
47: | 11-18 14:09 | GUI-Owl's MobileWorld model server killed by out-of-memory (prompt cache) | Run 1 discarded; run 2 with `--cache-ram 0` |
48: | 11-19 00:35–08:06 | Emulator 2 hung; 113 v4 seed-1234 episodes crashed in setup | Preregistered single re-run on emulator 1 with a liveness guard ([`aw_emu_guard.sh`](../scripts/androidworld/aw_emu_guard.sh)) |
49: | 11-19 04:57 | GCP VM stopped at its 12-h limit; MobileWorld containers vanished (`docker run --rm`) | Containers recreated with the original command |
50: | 11-19 10:30 | Restarted container's emulator refused to boot (stale AVD locks) | Graceful emulator stop + lock cleanup before every restart |
51: | 11-19 12:40 | First Colab model session hit its 24-h limit | Failover session with identical files (SHA-256), build and flags took over in 1 s |
52: | 11-19 12:42, 14:29 | Two spot-VM preemptions during MAI-UI's run | Watcher restarted the VM, recreated containers, re-ran interrupted tasks |
53: | 11-19 (MAI-UI run) | Emulators died 17 times with a fatal KVM error | Disclosed; affected tasks reported as a sensitivity analysis |
54: 
55: Full details and timing: dated entries in [PREREG_v4.md](PREREG_v4.md).
56: 
57: ---
58: 
59: ## Lessons
60: 
61: | Lesson | Applied as |
62: |---|---|
63: | Episode counts hide total failure | Watch exception counts and emulator liveness during sealed runs, not just progress |
64: | `--rm` containers vanish on VM stop | Recreate containers from the original command; stop emulators gracefully |
65: | Prompt caches distort speed and memory | Disable or exclude cached calls in benchmarks |
66: | Paid runs fail late | Smoke-test the full pipeline first; persist outputs as you go |
