11: 
12: ## AndroidWorld, held-out seeds (primary)
13: 
14: Preregistered comparison ([PREREG_v4.md](PREREG_v4.md)): 116 tasks × seeds 7, 1234, 2026; one run per model per seed.
15: Source: [`results/sealed_analysis_final.md`](../results/sealed_analysis_final.md) (+ `.json`).
16: 
17: ### Scores
18: 
19: | Model | Seed 7 | Seed 1234 | Seed 2026 | Total / 348 | Answer tasks / 75 | Action tasks / 273 |
20: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
21: | **LFM3-VL-2B v4** | 18 | 17 | 19 | **54 (15.5%)** | 13 | 41 |
22: | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (matched) | 16 | 13 | 18 | 47 (13.5%) | 19 | 28 |
23: | LFM3-VL-2B v1 | 11 | 10 | 11 | 32 (9.2%) | 0 | 32 |
24: 
25: - Success = AndroidWorld's checker says the task is done **and** the agent ended the episode.
26: - Exceptions count as failures.
27: - "Answer tasks" (25 per seed) need a typed answer; v1 never learned to answer.
28: 
29: ### Comparisons (paired, template-clustered sign-flip test, 10,000 draws)
30: 
31: | Comparison | Difference | 95% CI | p | Verdict |
32: |---|---|---|---|---|
33: | **v4 − GUI-Owl (primary)** | **+2.0 pts** | [−4.5, +8.6] | 0.60 | **Non-inferior** (lower bound > −6.9); not superior |
34: | v4 − v1 | +6.3 pts | [+1.1, +11.5] | 0.02 | v4 better |
35: | v1 − GUI-Owl | −4.3 pts | [−10.6, +1.9] | 0.21 | No significant difference |
36: 
37: Per-seed exact McNemar tests for v4 − GUI-Owl: p = 0.85, 0.52 and 1.0. No single seed is significant.
38: 
39: ### Sensitivity analyses
40: 
41: Source: [`results/sealed_sensitivity_final.md`](../results/sealed_sensitivity_final.md). None of these was preregistered.
42: 
43: | Variant | v4 | GUI-Owl | Difference | 95% CI | Non-inferior? |
44: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
45: | A. Primary | 54 | 47 | +2.0 | [−4.5, +8.6] | yes |
46: | B. Drop the 7 pairs that still end in an exception | 54 | 44 | +2.9 | [−3.4, +9.3] | yes |
47: | B3. Drop the 3 templates with non-setup exceptions (all seeds) | 54 | 43 | +3.2 | [−3.1, +9.6] | yes |
48: | **C. Count v4 seed 1234's 113 re-runs as failures** | 37 | 47 | **−2.9** | [−8.4, +2.7] | **no** |
49: | D. Exclude seed 1234 | 37 | 34 | +1.3 | [−5.8, +8.4] | yes |
50: | Disputed checker successes counted as failures | 53 | 47 | +1.7 | [−4.8, +8.3] | yes |
51: 
52: **Key point:** only variant C fails. In C, the preregistered "re-run once if the emulator crashed before step 1"
53: rule is not applied to v4's seed-1234 episodes. Emulator 2 hung from 00:35 to 08:06 on 2026-11-19, and every v4
54: seed-1234 episode in that window crashed during task setup.
55: 
56: ### Secondary breakdowns (preregistered, subordinate to the primary result)
57: 
58: Development seed 30 was used to choose v4. Templates whose goal text cannot change with the seed are therefore less
59: "held-out" than the others.
60: 
61: | Subset (3 seeds) | v4 | GUI-Owl | Difference | 95% CI | Non-inferior? |
62: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
63: | 78 templates whose goal text varies with the seed | 32 / 234 | 33 / 234 | −0.4 pts | [−8.2, +7.3] | **no** |
64: | 38 templates whose goal text is fixed (20 still vary hidden setup) | 22 / 114 | 14 / 114 | +7.0 pts | [−5.0, +19.1] | yes |
65: 
66: - **v4's overall lead comes from the 38 fixed-goal templates.** On the 78 seed-varying templates v4 and GUI-Owl are
67:   level, and non-inferiority is not established there.
68: 
69: | Difficulty (instances) | v4 | GUI-Owl | v1 |
70: |---|---|---|---|
71: | Easy (183) | 50 | 33 | 30 |
72: | Medium (108) | 3 | 11 | 0 |
73: | Hard (57) | 1 | 3 | 2 |
74: 
75: - v4 wins on easy tasks; GUI-Owl solves more medium and hard ones.
76: 
77: Source: rows E/F of [`results/sealed_sensitivity_final.md`](../results/sealed_sensitivity_final.md); difficulty
78: counts from [`results/sealed_analysis_final.md`](../results/sealed_analysis_final.md).
79: 
80: ### Re-runs and exceptions
81: 
82: | Arm | Episodes re-run once (setup crash before step 1) | Still an exception after re-run |
83: |---|---|---|
84: | v4 | seed 7: 4 · seed 1234: 113 | seed 1234: 4 (counted as failures) |
85: | GUI-Owl | seed 7: 1 · seed 1234: 1 · seed 2026: 2 | none |
86: | v1 | seed 2026: 1 | none |
87: 
88: Not re-run, counted as failures (the crash was not before step 1): v4 seed 1234 BrowserDraw,
89: v4 seed 2026 SimpleSmsReplyMostRecent, GUI-Owl seed 1234 SimpleSmsSendReceivedAddress.
90: 
91: ### Disputed checker successes
92: 
93: Checker successes were compared with their saved screenshots: all v4 and GUI-Owl successes, and v1's on seeds 1234
94: and 2026 (122 of 133; v1's 11 seed-7 successes have no review record). Two contradict the screens. They stay
95: successes in the primary score and count as failures only in the sensitivity row above.
96: 
97: | Arm | Seed | Task | Why disputed |
98: |---|---|---|---|
99: | v4 | 7 | ClockStopWatchPausedVerify | Stopwatch left running |
100: | v1 | 2026 | OpenAppTaskEval | Opened Contacts, then deleted the only contact before finishing |
101: 
102: Source: [`results/aw_checker_disputes.json`](../results/aw_checker_disputes.json).
103: 
104: ### Known limits
105: 
106: - **Device state is not fully reset between episodes (all models).** AndroidWorld's app-snapshot restore is
107:   skipped ("Snapshot not found"), so data a task's own setup does not clear can carry over. Bias direction is unknown.
108: - **Power is limited.** Cluster standard error is about 3.25 points. Detecting superiority with 80% power would need
109:   about a 9-point true gap.
110: - **A harness defect affects all models:** gRPC warnings on adb's error output can corrupt adb replies during task
111:   setup. Those crashes fall under the re-run rule.
112: - **The interval is nominal.** The 95% CI comes from inverting the sign-flip test, so it assumes symmetric paired
113:   differences and exact coverage is not guaranteed.
114: - **GUI-Owl runs in our harness, not its own.** It gets one screenshot at ≤ 1,048,576 pixels and 4-bit weights,
115:   not its published configuration of 5 screenshots and full resolution. Its published AndroidWorld score is 67.9%.
116: 
