11: | MAI-UI-2B | 2 | 1063.1 (1062.8–1063.4) | 1061.0 s | 3,032 (462 cached) | 1058.4 s | 58 | 22 | 2/2 | 2.65 |
12: 
13: **Option 2: all three with the same configured 1,024-token image ceiling** (a speed comparison at an equal ceiling, not verified equal image tokens; GUI-Owl's and MAI-UI's accuracy at this budget was not measured), 5 screenshots, pass 1 v4 → GUI-Owl → MAI-UI, pass 2 reversed:
14: 
15: | Model (pass) | Timed calls | Seconds per step, end-to-end (median, range) | On the phone (median) | Prompt tokens | Prompt time on the phone (incl. image encoding) | Output tokens | Output tokens/s | Finished normally | Fastest core, sampled GHz |
16: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
17: | **v4 (ours)** (1) | 5 | **39.2** (38.3–41.3) | 36.9 s | 1,081 (0 cached) | 36.2 s | 28 | 41 | 5/5 | 2.65 |
18: | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (1) | 5 | 197.8 (197.0–198.5) | 195.4 s | 1,982 (973 cached) | 193.9 s | 44 | 31 | 5/5 | 2.65 |
19: | MAI-UI-2B (1) | 5 | 183.2 (182.9–184.0) | 181.2 s | 1,460 (446 cached) | 179.0 s | 60 | 28 | 5/5 | 2.65 |
20: | **v4 (ours)** (2) | 5 | **38.8** (37.7–39.0) | 36.9 s | 1,081 (0 cached) | 36.2 s | 28 | 42 | 5/5 | 2.65 |
21: | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (2) | 5 | 197.4 (197.1–197.5) | 195.4 s | 1,982 (973 cached) | 193.9 s | 44 | 31 | 5/5 | 2.65 |
22: | MAI-UI-2B (2) | 5 | 183.3 (182.7–184.3) | 181.3 s | 1,460 (446 cached) | 179.2 s | 60 | 28 | 5/5 | 2.65 |
23: 
24: Round 1 (earlier the same day, default flash-attention setting, 3 timed passes): v4 completed all 15 timed calls, median 28.8 s end-to-end (26.9 s on the phone). GUI-Owl's and MAI-UI's first calls never completed before their client gave up (MobileWorld's 120 s timeout plus re-sends), so round 2 raised the OpenAI client timeout to 3,600 s with SDK re-sends off (v4's own client: 300 s); every round-2 call completed on its first request. A single MAI-UI Q4_K_M probe with flash attention took 1176.1 s (1066.2 s on the prompt) and ended in a 2048-token degenerate output (finish reason `length`).
25: 
26: The phone slowed under sustained load: after about two hours the sampled fastest-core frequency had fallen from 4.03 GHz to about 2.65 GHz (medians of sampled maxima, not controlled clocks) and v4's same screenshots went from ~27 s to ~38 s; that is why option 2 runs the models in both orders. Raw requests, thermal samples and server logs: working repo `results/qdc/`.
