+
+**Scope and decision.** Audited branch restructure at d76fec421e9a09377e0eae6d96b8522df2884b4f, including fix commit be7bc11. Of F02–F31, **24 are fixed, 5 partly fixed, and 1 not fixed**. Five new findings are listed above. The corrected measured results hold up; merge readiness still depends on the bounded code/documentation fixes. F01 remains the owner's explicitly deferred identity/history decision and is not counted as a new blocker in this re-audit. F02's remote replacement was not attempted or inferred.
+
+N01 is a static startup-race exposure, not an assertion that recorded runs collided: when an absolute-path launcher has started but has not yet created its runner/server, the lane can miss its ownership. A successful cd changes the working directory, not the process command line. N02 restores the old functionality, but also restores the older launcher's known hang path. These operational scripts were never launched during this audit.
+
+**Reproduction and read-only handling.** To obey the rule that every write remain inside this audit folder, the exact command `bash analysis/reproduce.sh` ran in a disposable snapshot containing the 8,940 tracked paths. Git comparisons used the original HEAD/object database with a copied index and the snapshot as GIT_WORK_TREE; no ref or original index was changed.
+
+- **Tracked inputs only:** exit 0, about 24.7 s, no AndroidWorld clone, MobileWorld correctly skipped. [Output](reproduce.log), [state](reproduce_state.json).
+- **With the existing local MobileWorld trajectories:** exit 0, about 3.3 s, raw inputs read through child symlinks inside the ignored trajectory directory; all outputs remained in the snapshot. [Output](reproduce_with_mobileworld.log), [state](reproduce_with_mobileworld_state.json).
+- Both successful runs ended: “OK: every regenerated file is identical to the committed one (HEAD), and no new file appeared.” Both snapshot statuses were clean.
+- An initial whole-directory trajectory symlink was itself untracked because the ignore rule applies to directories. That audit-harness attempt failed only the final status check; its log/state are retained as the *_symlink_probe files. Replacing it with an ignored real directory containing read-only input links gave the successful full run above.
+- The actual checkout's final-check fragment was tested separately: tracked result diff = 0, but the authorized audit folder alone makes the blanket status predicate false. This is N03, not a claim that an in-place reproduction ended OK.
+- The snapshot, copied index and temporary analysis outputs were removed after verification. The final original-checkout hashes, status and refs are recorded in [final_state.json](final_state.json).
+
+**Independent numerical checks.** The audit reran its own episode/prediction/log counting code rather than accepting the fix message or regenerated tables as numerical evidence. It also rescored all seven available canonical AndroidControl prediction files and checked all eight paired retention reports. The missing older canonical raw prediction files remain a limit on “every number” claims.
+
+| Check | Independently derived result |
+|---|---|
+| Held-out totals, v4 / GUI-Owl / v1 | 54 / 47 / 32; per seed 18/17/19, 16/13/18, 11/10/11 |
+| Primary paired inference | +2.011494 pp; sign-flip p=0.602339766 |
+| E, varying-goal templates | 78 clusters, 234 instances; 32 vs 33; −0.427350 pp; p=1; CI [−8.108108,+7.207207] |
+| F, fixed-goal templates | 38 clusters, 114 instances; 22 vs 14; +7.017544 pp; p=0.311168883; CI [−5,+19.047619] |
+| Difficulty, v4 / GUI-Owl / v1 | Easy 50/33/30; medium 3/11/0; hard 1/3/2 |
+| v4 retention, MMStar | 793/1500 vs base 782/1500; 115 lost, 126 gained; p=0.519559247 |
+| v4 retention, MMLU | 504/1000 vs base 489/1000; 61 lost, 76 gained; p=0.231537166 |
+| CPU retained calls and medians, v4 / GUI-Owl / MAI-UI | 14/4/4; 6.398/57.997/58.1785 s |
+| Phone evaluation-budget GUI-Owl / MAI-UI | 2/2 calls; 1099.8285/1063.0695 s |
+| Phone equal-ceiling pass 1 / pass 2 | v4 39.201/38.757 s; GUI-Owl 197.780/197.365 s; MAI-UI 183.161/183.276 s; five calls per model per pass |
+| Pixel partial v4 | 11 calls; median 74.407 s |
+| RL log | 200 steps; mean zero-variance fraction 0.663125; first/last 20-step rewards 0.71352/0.765095 |
+
+Evidence: [recomputed_evidence.json](recomputed_evidence.json), [numeric_checks.json](numeric_checks.json), [training_and_exception_details.json](training_and_exception_details.json), [audit_times.json](audit_times.json). The two new E/F rows use the same unmodified primary-analysis functions; independent breakpoint inversion agrees with their exact endpoints and outward rounding. The new v4 retention artifact regenerated byte-identically, including its bootstrap intervals.
+
+The seed-30 mutation checks distinguish the corrected score predicate from still-incomplete input validation. A success with non-null exception now scores zero. Wrong seed, duplicate template and one differing agent are rejected. Uniform wrong agents, uniformly missing agents, missing instance_id, two records per file and seedless after-step exceptions are accepted. Current present seeds agree with suite seed 30, and all current instance IDs are 0. Thirteen current non-setup exception records lack a stored seed, so a complete provenance check needs an explicit run-level record; it must not invent missing per-episode metadata. See [probes.json](probes.json).
+
+**File integrity, inventory and documentation.**
+
+| Check | Result |
+|---|---|
+| Pinned AndroidWorld metadata | Byte-identical to both local android_world/android_world/task_metadata.json and git object 55ddaf5:android_world/task_metadata.json; 116 templates; SHA-256 fd3cf23ebb26e461a961dd60ff3f011d7e6ec78c992c10babbbdb86f9dd591e1 |
+| Local AndroidWorld commit | 55ddaf5edc6f6c25673aed343907d5b9dca66f84 |
+| PREREG | Byte-identical to archive/pre-restructure-2026-11-20; SHA-256 e018283e788e754f0192177c4d5c9d1a3a08a18328c12ffc79cd9b46cdbdd35a |
+| Changed shell syntax/root derivation | 24/24 syntax checks; 72/72 isolated root checks, covering root-relative and absolute/relative invocation from another working directory |
+| Operational move counts | analysis 11; AndroidWorld 20; MobileWorld 13; training 32; training jobs 30; speed 10; publishing 6; research reports 2; research notes 11; history document 1 |
+| Additional rename in requested diff | One archived registry-source copy, N05 |
+| Removed groups | Logs 58 files; dataset scratch 224 files / 354,445,648 bytes; VM backups 36 files / 10,966,053 bytes; all declared deletion paths accounted for |
+| Backup preservation | Every removed VM-backup blob has an identical surviving canonical file; mappings retained in static_checks.json |
+| Remaining fixture duplication | Eight pass3 copies, 31,010,776 total checkout bytes, F30 |
+| Documentation/link review | README.md and all nine non-PREREG top-level docs read in full; 197 local/cached-object links and anchors checked with no broken destination; three research rewrites preserve prose |
+
+The archive comparison is captured in [changes.tsv](changes.tsv), generated from `git diff --name-status -M archive/pre-restructure-2026-11-20 HEAD`. Detailed checks: [identity.json](identity.json), [static_checks.json](static_checks.json), [links.json](links.json), [launchers.json](launchers.json). The remaining prose issues are identified in F02, F07, F24 and N04; the tables identified by F29 are now readable.
+
+**Added-blob secret scan.** Scanned the full HEAD postimages selected by `git diff ecdebc5 HEAD`: **90 paths, 89 unique blobs, 7,803,007 bytes**. No added/modified blob was gzip-compressed; the scanner detects gzip by magic and decompresses it when present. It also checks escaped quoted assignments in captured tool text.
+
+No recognized credential or owner-email match was found. Twenty broad assignment candidates were inspected/classified: seven numerical metric strings, six redaction placeholders, and seven synthetic test values. Candidate artifacts contain only a prefix of at most six characters, length and SHA-256—not full values. Patterns cover common provider tokens, cloud access keys, JWTs, private-key headers, credential URLs/query parameters, bearer tokens, quoted assignments, recognized unquoted environment assignments, and the owner's actual metadata address.
+
+[added_blob_scan.json](added_blob_scan.json) records the exact blob inventory and masked candidates; [scan_added.py](scan_added.py) records the procedure. This is an added-blob scan, not a new all-history or live-remote clean bill. Existing F01 metadata/history exposure is deliberately outside the requested fix decision, and no images were OCR-scanned.
+
+No network, push, commit, ref change, process signal, emulator, adb or cloud command was used. Operational scripts were inspected and syntax/pattern-tested only.
+
